{"name":"Sail","hex":"#a5ceec","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sail","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A piece of fabric attached to a boat and arranged such that it causes the wind to drive the boat along. The sail may be attached to the boat via a combination of mast, spars and ropes.","The concept of a sail or sails, as if a substance."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be impelled or driven forward by the action of wind upon sails, as a ship on water; to be impelled on a body of water by steam or other power.","To move through or on the water; to swim, as a fish or a waterfowl."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sail"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sail","blocks":[{"text":"A sail is a tensile structure, which is made from fabric or other membrane materials, that uses wind power to propel sailing craft, including sailing ships, sailboats, windsurfers, ice boats, and even sail-powered land vehicles. Sails may be made from a combination of woven materials—including canvas or polyester cloth, laminated membranes or bonded filaments, usually in a three- or four-sided shape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Chesapeake.jpg/330px-Chesapeake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sail"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg/500px-Sailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Sailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg/500px-Sailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASailing_Vessel_Odyssey.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg/250px-L-2013-Oracle-Team-USA-17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikiped